       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for prescription use in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum, and it is usually for short-term use.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day). These are common choices for pain or inflammation.\n- **1,600 mg/day as a single daily total**, if the intended figure was the daily dose rather than the per-dose amount.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If the 1,600 mg figure was a typo, for example for 600 mg or 800 mg, let me know. If you need more analgesia than the maximum allows, consider adding acetaminophen or another agent. I can enter that too."
      }
