      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Confirming that the dose is intentional doesn't change the limit. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and 6,400 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day. I won't enter a dose above that maximum based on a statement alone.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the labeled maximum.\n- **A lower dose**, such as 600 mg four times daily, if you prefer.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, the usual route is to discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. Pharmacy can review it and, if it's justified, process it through your institution's override process. I'd also look at adding a different agent, such as acetaminophen, instead of raising the ibuprofen dose.\n\nTell me if you want one of the in-range orders entered."
      }
     ],
